Spring Cloud Stream's Kafka Streams binder lets you declare topology functions and configure them via properties. A representative flow: enrich incoming `clicks` (KStream) with `users` (KTable, partitioned by userId) and `countries` (GlobalKTable, broadcast lookup), then aggregate per country in 5-minute tumbling windows.

```java
@Configuration
public class ClickAnalyticsTopology {

    @Bean
    public Function<KStream<String, Click>,
                    Function<KTable<String, User>,
                    Function<GlobalKTable<String, Country>,
                             KStream<Windowed<String>, Long>>>>
            enrichAndCount() {
        return clicks -> users -> countries -> clicks
            // KStream-KTable join: clicks must be co-partitioned with users (same key, same partitions).
            .leftJoin(users, (click, user) ->
                user == null ? click : click.withUser(user))

            // KStream-GlobalKTable join: no co-partitioning required;
            // we look up country by user.countryCode (any field, not the stream key).
            .leftJoin(countries,
                (clickKey, click) -> click.user() == null ? null : click.user().countryCode(),
                (click, country) -> click.withCountry(country))

            .filter((k, v) -> v.country() != null)

            // Re-key by country code so the aggregation is co-partitioned by country.
            .selectKey((k, v) -> v.country().code())
            .groupByKey(Grouped.with(Serdes.String(), clickSerde()))

            .windowedBy(TimeWindows
                .ofSizeAndGrace(Duration.ofMinutes(5), Duration.ofMinutes(2)))
            .count(Materialized.as("clicks-per-country-5m"))
            .toStream();
    }

    private Serde<Click> clickSerde() { /* JSON / Avro serde */ }
}
```

```yaml
spring:
  cloud:
    stream:
      function:
        definition: enrichAndCount
      bindings:
        enrichAndCount-in-0:   { destination: clicks }
        enrichAndCount-in-1:   { destination: users }
        enrichAndCount-in-2:   { destination: countries }
        enrichAndCount-out-0:  { destination: clicks-per-country-5m }
      kafka:
        streams:
          binder:
            applicationId: click-analytics
            configuration:
              processing.guarantee: exactly_once_v2
              num.stream.threads: 4
              state.dir: /var/lib/streams
          bindings:
            enrichAndCount-in-1: { consumer: { materializedAs: users-store } }
            enrichAndCount-in-2: { consumer: { materializedAs: countries-store } }
```

The `Materialized.as("clicks-per-country-5m")` call gives the windowed aggregation a queryable state store name that you can query interactively from the Spring app via `KafkaStreams.store(...)` for low-latency dashboards backed by the local RocksDB store.
